# Frontend Standards

## Unified Planner

- One operational calendar page with a right-side drawer (tabs): Summary, Requests, Proposals, Assignments, Incidents.

- Two modes (toggle): PLANNING (capacity view) / ASSIGNMENTS (people view).

- Event color legend: UNCOVERED(red), PROPOSED(amber), CONFIRMED(blue), ASSIGNED(blue-dark), IN_PROGRESS(green), CLOSED(gray).

## UX

- Actions: create slot/WO, send staffing request, review/accept proposals, assign, substitute, split/merge shifts.

- Batch operations: select multiple slots; send request/assign in bulk.

- No `alert/confirm/fetch` direct calls. Use `ApiClient`, `Toast`, `ConfirmDialog`.

- Accessible (labels, focus-visible, ARIA), responsive (drawer full-screen on mobile).

## Routing

- Calendar is the hub for Empresa; do not create a second calendar page.

- Agency has its own calendar showing only its workers' shifts.

## No dead code / no duplication

- Remove/merge former isolated pages into the unified planner.
